{
  "type": "excalidraw",
  "version": 2,
  "source": "https://excalidraw.com",
  "elements": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "x": 140,
      "y": 10,
      "width": 520,
      "height": 35,
      "strokeColor": "#f0f6fc",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "🔍  TypeVar explained — the \"ModelT\" mystery",
      "fontSize": 22,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "title",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 2,
      "x": 100,
      "y": 45,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 20,
      "strokeColor": "#8b949e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "The line:  ModelT = TypeVar(\"ModelT\", bound=BaseModel)",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "subtitle",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 3,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 740,
      "height": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#8b949e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "Let's start with the problem — then see how TypeVar solves it:",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "intro",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "x": 40,
      "y": 110,
      "width": 720,
      "height": 60,
      "strokeColor": "#f85149",
      "backgroundColor": "#f8514911",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "rectangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "x": 50,
      "y": 115,
      "width": 700,
      "height": 50,
      "strokeColor": "#f85149",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "❌ The problem:\n\n_validate_model(FunctionDefinition, data) should return → list[FunctionDefinition]\n_validate_model(PromptItem, data)      should return → list[PromptItem]\n\nBut if you write the return type as → list[BaseModel], mypy doesn't know WHICH subclass.\nIt loses the specific type information — you get a generic BaseModel back, not FunctionDefinition.",
      "fontSize": 9,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "problem",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 2,
      "x": 40,
      "y": 190,
      "width": 720,
      "height": 65,
      "strokeColor": "#3fb950",
      "backgroundColor": "#3fb95011",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "rectangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 2,
      "x": 50,
      "y": 195,
      "width": 700,
      "height": 55,
      "strokeColor": "#3fb950",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "✅ The solution — Generics / TypeVar:\n\nTypeVar creates a \"placeholder type\" that gets filled in at the call site.\nWhen you call _validate_model(FunctionDefinition, data), the T becomes FunctionDefinition.\nWhen you call _validate_model(PromptItem, data), the T becomes PromptItem.\nmypy tracks this automatically.",
      "fontSize": 9,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "solution",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 4,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 280,
      "width": 740,
      "height": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#8b949e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "Breaking down the line piece by piece:",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "breakdown-title",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 3,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 305,
      "width": 180,
      "height": 55,
      "strokeColor": "#f0883e",
      "backgroundColor": "#f0883e22",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "boundElements": [{ "type": "text", "id": "part1" }],
      "elementType": "rectangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 2,
      "x": 35,
      "y": 308,
      "width": 170,
      "height": 50,
      "strokeColor": "#f0883e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "ModelT\n\nThis is just a variable name.\nCould be T, ItemType, anything.\nBy convention: T or ModelT.",
      "fontSize": 9,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "id": "part1",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 4,
      "x": 240,
      "y": 305,
      "width": 180,
      "height": 55,
      "strokeColor": "#a371f7",
      "backgroundColor": "#a371f722",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "boundElements": [{ "type": "text", "id": "part2" }],
      "elementType": "rectangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 3,
      "x": 245,
      "y": 308,
      "width": 170,
      "height": 50,
      "strokeColor": "#a371f7",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "= TypeVar(...)\n\nTypeVar is a function from\ntyping module.\nIt creates a \"type variable\"\n— a placeholder for a real type.",
      "fontSize": 9,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "id": "part2",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 5,
      "x": 450,
      "y": 305,
      "width": 180,
      "height": 55,
      "strokeColor": "#58a6ff",
      "backgroundColor": "#58a6ff22",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "boundElements": [{ "type": "text", "id": "part3" }],
      "elementType": "rectangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 3,
      "x": 455,
      "y": 308,
      "width": 170,
      "height": 50,
      "strokeColor": "#58a6ff",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "\"ModelT\"\n\nThe name string. Used for\nrepr/debug. Should match\nthe variable name.\nmypy uses this in error msgs.",
      "fontSize": 9,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "id": "part3",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 6,
      "x": 660,
      "y": 305,
      "width": 110,
      "height": 55,
      "strokeColor": "#3fb950",
      "backgroundColor": "#3fb95022",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "boundElements": [{ "type": "text", "id": "part4" }],
      "elementType": "rectangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 3,
      "x": 665,
      "y": 308,
      "width": 100,
      "height": 50,
      "strokeColor": "#3fb950",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "bound=BaseModel\n\nThe constraint: ModelT can\nONLY be BaseModel or a\nsubclass of BaseModel.",
      "fontSize": 9,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "id": "part4",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "line",
      "version": 1,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 380,
      "width": 740,
      "height": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#30363d",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "points": [[0, 0], [740, 0]],
      "elementType": "line"
    },

    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 5,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 395,
      "width": 740,
      "height": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#8b949e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "🔍 Why bound=BaseModel? Without it, TypeVar accepts ANY type — even str, int, etc.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "why-bound",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 7,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 420,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 90,
      "strokeColor": "#f85149",
      "backgroundColor": "#f8514911",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "rectangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 4,
      "x": 35,
      "y": 425,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 80,
      "strokeColor": "#f85149",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "❌ WITHOUT bound=BaseModel:\n\nT = TypeVar(\"T\")\ndef validate(model_type: type[T], data) → T: ...\n\nvalidate(str, \"hello\") → returns str   ← mypy allows this!\nvalidate(int, 42)      → returns int   ← mypy allows this!\n\nThe function would accept ANY type, not just Pydantic models.",
      "fontSize": 8,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "without-bound",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 8,
      "x": 420,
      "y": 420,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 90,
      "strokeColor": "#3fb950",
      "backgroundColor": "#3fb95011",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "rectangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 5,
      "x": 425,
      "y": 425,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 80,
      "strokeColor": "#3fb950",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "✅ WITH bound=BaseModel:\n\nT = TypeVar(\"T\", bound=BaseModel)\ndef validate(model_type: type[T], data) → T: ...\n\nvalidate(FunctionDefinition, data) → FD  ← mypy knows this\nvalidate(PromptItem, data)         → PI  ← mypy knows this\nvalidate(str, \"hello\")              → ❌ mypy rejects: str is not a BaseModel",
      "fontSize": 8,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "with-bound",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "line",
      "version": 2,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 530,
      "width": 740,
      "height": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#30363d",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "points": [[0, 0], [740, 0]],
      "elementType": "line"
    },

    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 6,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 545,
      "width": 740,
      "height": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#8b949e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "📊 Now see how ModelT is used in the actual function:",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "usage-title",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 9,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 570,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 55,
      "strokeColor": "#d29922",
      "backgroundColor": "#d2992211",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "rectangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 5,
      "x": 70,
      "y": 575,
      "width": 660,
      "height": 45,
      "strokeColor": "#d29922",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "def _validate_model(model_type: type[ModelT], data: Any) -> ModelT:\n    validator = getattr(model_type, \"model_validate\", None)\n    if callable(validator):\n        return validator(data)         # Pydantic v2\n    return model_type.parse_obj(data)   # Pydantic v1 fallback",
      "fontSize": 9,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "id": "usage-code",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 6,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 635,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 40,
      "strokeColor": "#8b949e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "▸ model_type: type[ModelT]  → the first argument is a CLASS (not an instance), and that class must be a BaseModel subclass\n▸ data: Any                  → the raw dict/list to validate\n▸ → ModelT                   → returns an instance of whatever class was passed in\n▸ getattr(model_type, \"model_validate\", None)  → checks if the class has a model_validate method (Pydantic v2 feature)\n▸ If it does → use v2. If not → fall back to parse_obj (Pydantic v1 compatibility)",
      "fontSize": 8,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "usage-explanation",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "line",
      "version": 3,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 740,
      "height": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#30363d",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "points": [[0, 0], [740, 0]],
      "elementType": "line"
    },

    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 7,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 705,
      "width": 740,
      "height": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#8b949e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "💡  In action — what mypy sees vs what you'd get without TypeVar:",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "action-title",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 10,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 730,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 70,
      "strokeColor": "#58a6ff",
      "backgroundColor": "#58a6ff11",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "rectangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 6,
      "x": 35,
      "y": 735,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 60,
      "strokeColor": "#58a6ff",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "✅ With TypeVar (current code):\n\nfns = _validate_model(FunctionDefinition, data)\n# mypy knows: fns is FunctionDefinition\n# autocomplete works: fns.name, fns.description\n\nprs = _validate_model(PromptItem, data)\n# mypy knows: prs is PromptItem\n# autocomplete: prs.prompt",
      "fontSize": 8,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "with-tvar",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 11,
      "x": 420,
      "y": 730,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 70,
      "strokeColor": "#f85149",
      "backgroundColor": "#f8514911",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "rectangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 6,
      "x": 425,
      "y": 735,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 60,
      "strokeColor": "#f85149",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "❌ Without TypeVar (returning BaseModel):\n\nfns = validate(FunctionDefinition, data)\n# mypy thinks: fns is BaseModel\n# no autocomplete: .name, .description\n# must cast to use subclass methods\n\nprs = validate(PromptItem, data)\n# mypy thinks: prs is BaseModel\n# same problem",
      "fontSize": 8,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "without-tvar",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    },

    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 8,
      "x": 30,
      "y": 820,
      "width": 740,
      "height": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#8b949e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "🧠  Analogy: TypeVar is like a placeholder in a template. \"Give me a BaseModel subclass → I'll give you back that same type, with full type info preserved.\"",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "id": "analogy",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "elementType": "text"
    }
  ],
  "appState": {
    "gridSize": null,
    "viewBackgroundColor": "#0d1117"
  }
}
